sound E1L.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I burned it.
music BGM16B.mp3
text That's what Kotomi says.
text It almost sounds like she says it with a laugh.
text I remember this part.
text In my hazy memory, one image still remains clear.
text A small girl crying in the middle of the room.
text Orange flames flicking like a snake's tongue.
text @[Tomoya]
text Why did you do that?
sound E1M.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I don't know.
sound E1N.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I don't know...
text She's at a loss for words.
text I look at the colossal stack of cut-out pages scattered on the floor.
text @[Tomoya]
text Did you cut out all of these?
text Still looking away, she nods.
sound E1O.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text At first, I did it to atone.
sound E1P.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text In place of what I burned, I cut out all of the newspaper articles that mentioned my mother and father.
sound E1Q.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text But I thought that wasn't enough.
if intF[403] == 0
	goto s60
fi
goto 60
label s60
text I remember when I met Kotomi at the bookstore in front of the station.
text She must have been making her rounds to the bookstores since she was small.
text She must have had to stand on her toes to get the technical books on physics that were high up on the shelves.
text She must have turned the pages as best she could with her tiny fingers.
text She would read through entire books without even knowing the meanings of the technical terms.
text She did all of that to find the fragments of what remained of her parents.
goto 61
label 60
if intF[403] == 1
	goto s61
fi
goto 61
label s61
text I think back to when I first met Kotomi at the library.
text She looked as if she had been deep in thought, almost in prayer, with the scissors in her hand.
label 61
sound E1R.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I would get so happy when I found my mother and father's names.
sound E1S.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It felt like they were talking to me.
sound E1T.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I wanted to buy the books, but they were all so expensive...
sound E1U.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text That's why I took out my scissors and...
sound E1V.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I apologized in my heart, saying, "I'm sorry. I know it hurts."
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
sound E1W.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I've studied the best I could ever since.
sound E1X.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Studying was very fun.
sound E1Y.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I thought that I would understand my father's books and papers.
sound E1Z.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I thought that it would let me hear my father's voice.
sound E20.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text But my father's books were very, very difficult.
sound E21.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Just reading the words didn't make me understand them.
sound E22.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I couldn't understand them without knowing more about the world.
sound E23.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text That's why I studied more and more...
sound E24.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I read more and more books...
sound E25.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I wanted to take over from where my mother and father left off.
text I didn't know this side of Kotomi, dryly talking about herself.
text Kotomi must be teaching herself stuff at the forefront of academics. Stuff they don't even teach at universities.
text There's no way the classes at our school would teach it.
text That's why Kotomi has to study on her own, all the while trying her best to be more like her parents.
text That's why she reads books voraciously at the library instead of going to class.
text She goes home after school instead of hanging out with people. After going home, she studies more difficult things alone.
text @[Tomoya]
text Kotomi...
text I can't say it.
text That this is all so sad.
sound E26.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text They told me.
sound E27.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text The papers were irreplaceable.
sound E28.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text They said they were worth more than my mother and father's lives.
sound E29.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text That can't be true.
sound E2A.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text There's nothing more valuable than my mother and father's lives.
sound E2B.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I will never forget.
sound E2C.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I can't forget.
text With her head down, she bites her lip.
sound E2D.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text But...
sound E2E.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I'm close to understanding my mother and father's research.
sound E2F.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text They were trying to explain the origin of the world using the most beautiful words possible.
sound E2G.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text They were going to spend their lives together trying to find those words.
sound E2H.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It must be something very important.
sound E2I.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It's something that should be told to everyone in the world.
sound E2J.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It was something only my mother and father could do.
sound E2K.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It's something that no one else can imitate...
sound E2L.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It must be something even I can't imitate...
sound E2M.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text But unless I do it...
sound E2N.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text God... won't forgive me.
text Kotomi stops talking.
text No matter how much she studies... no matter how many books she reads...
text She's still a small child afraid of the outside world.
text She's still the desperate little girl who just burned something precious.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text Maybe I should sit down next to her.
text Maybe I should say I'm here for her.
text Just like how Kotomi wanted me to do when she was small.
text Even now, that probably hasn't changed.
text The other Kotomi inside of her will refuse to leave this place.
text That's why...
text There's only one thing I can say.
text @[Tomoya]
text Come to school tomorrow.
text Kotomi's shoulders twitch.
sound E2O.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I don't want to go...
sound E2P.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I can't take it anymore...
text She says that in a raspy, almost inaudible voice.
sound E2Q.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I don't want to feel that sad anymore...
text Kotomi must have flashed back to her past when she heard that Fujibayashi might have gotten into an accident.
text Just like how her parents disappeared without warning on that day.
text And she still remembers the promise she made to God that isn't fulfilled yet.
text What I'm asking from Kotomi might be something very cruel.
text But even so, I have to repeat it.
text @[Tomoya]
text Come to school tomorrow.
text @[Tomoya]
text You'd better come.
text @[Tomoya]
text I'll be waiting for you.
text @[Tomoya]
text Furukawa, Fujibayashi, and Kyou... we'll all be waiting for you.
text @[Tomoya]
text Goodbye, Kotomi.
text @[Tomoya]
text See you tomorrow.
text I don't get a response.
text @[Tomoya]
text See you tomorrow.
text No answer.
text @[Tomoya]
text See you tomorrow.
sound E2R.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text ...
text I think I see her jaw move slightly.
text That must be the best she can do at the moment.
